From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:38:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [cellbroadcast] Keep suppressed and dismissed alerts down,
 check inputs.

- A geofencing trigger moved every suppressed alert it referenced to
  AwaitingLocation, including alerts suppressed because their channel is
  off, their display policy is "none" or they are another language's
  copy, so a location inside the area showed them. Only re-check those
  that are presentable.
- An acknowledged alert went back to a location check, and on screen,
  when the same update arrived in the preferred language with a
  different area. Only a newer update brings it back.
- CellBroadcastGeoFence::check() emitted resolved() before returning
  when the deadline had passed or no position source exists. That
  re-entered the daemon while it was storing an alert, after which it
  announced the active alert it had read before, so clients ended on a
  stale one. Deliver such answers from the event loop; a later check()
  or cancel() of the alert replaces them, and they replace an earlier
  pending request.
- A deadline more than 24.8 days ahead wrapped the timer interval to
  1 ms, which then fired and restarted location updates continuously.
- toDouble() accepts "nan" and "inf", for which the range checks all
  pass and the area test comes out Outside, suppressing the alert,
  instead of Invalid, which shows it. Require finite values.
- The attention sound was accepted on a prefix match alone, which
  "attention-tones/../.." passes. Compare the resolved path.

The store test ran without an application object, so its timers, and
QTest::qWait() in the geofence tests, never fired; it now uses
QTEST_GUILESS_MAIN.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
